<FullPage
  title="Novated Leases — An Independent Australian Guide & Calculator"
  description="Free independent Australian novated lease guide and calculator. Compare EV and ICE novated leases against cash purchase and car loan — based on real net outcomes, not misleading 'tax saved' figures."
>
  <div class="home-content">

    <!-- Two-column split: text left, calculator preview right -->
    <div class="home-hero-split">

      <!-- Left column -->
      <div class="home-hero-left">
        <div class="home-hero">
          <h1>Novated Lease Guide & Calculator</h1>

          <div class="home-cta-block">
            <div class="home-cta-row">
              <a href="/calculator/" class="home-cta-btn">Open the Calculator →</a>
              <a href="/tools/byo-employer-check/" class="home-cta-btn home-cta-btn--outline">Employer BYO Checker →</a>
            </div>
            <p class="home-cta-caption">Calculator models true net cost — not the inflated "tax saved" figure providers advertise.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <hr style="border:none;border-top:1px solid var(--color-border);margin:32px 0 28px;" />

        <div class="home-body">
          <p><strong>Many people dismiss EV novated leases for the wrong reasons</strong>, based on outdated rules of thumb rather than current rules.</p>
          <p><strong>Many people sign up for novated leases for the wrong reasons</strong>, based on misleading sales pitches rather than a clear understanding of costs, risks, and trade‑offs.</p>
          <p><strong>This site is written for both.</strong> The calculator is <a href="/start-here/calculator-comparison/">one of very few</a> that models true net savings — not the <a href="/costs-and-savings/false-saving-example/">misleading "tax saved" figure</a> most providers advertise. The accompanying articles cover the pros and cons in depth, written by someone with no affiliation with any leasing company and no financial interest in your decision.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="home-alert">
          <strong>🆕 Updated May 2026:</strong> The calculator and articles fully reflect the new EV FBT wind-back rules announced in the May 2026 Budget — including the 25% FBT discount applying from April 2027 for eligible EVs above $75,000. <a href="/special-and-policy/ev-fbt-exemption-phase-out-budget-2026/">Read the full explainer →</a>
        </div>
      </div><!-- /.home-hero-left -->

      <!-- Right column: example calculator result -->
